  Digital Forensic Report Format
  
  A good forensic report must be
  
  clear, concise, and admissible in court
  
  . It should follow a structured approach to ensure
  
  chain of custody
  
  , reproducibility, and credibility.
  
  1\. Cover Page
  
  
  
  Title:
  
  Digital Forensic Investigation Report
  
  
  
  Case Number / ID:
  
  
  
  Date:
  
  
  
  Prepared by:
  
  (Name, Designation)
  
  
  
  Organization:
  
  
  
  Confidentiality Statement:
  
  (“This report contains sensitive information intendedonly for authorized use.”)
  
  2
  
  . Table of Contents
  
  (Automatically generated if the report is long)
  
  3\. Execuve Summary
  
  
  
  Brief description of the case
  
  
  
  Objective of the investigation
  
  
  
  Key findings
  
  
  
  Conclusion (1–2 lines)
  
  4
  
  . Scope of Invesgaon
  
  
  
  Purpose (Why the investigation was initiated)
  
  
  
  Questions to answer (e.g., Was there unauthorized access? Who was responsible?)
  
  
  
  Legal authority (if applicable – warrant, corporate request)
  
  5\. Case Details
  
  
  
  Case Reference:
  
  
  
  Investigator(s):
  
  ![](https://html.scribdassets.com/97ebbo680fs0ulz/images/3-8121f45bc7.jpg)![](https://html.scribdassets.com/97ebbo680fs0ulz/images/3-8121f45bc7.jpg)![](https://html.scribdassets.com/97ebbo680fs0ulz/images/3-8121f45bc7.jpg)![](https://html.scribdassets.com/97ebbo680fs0ulz/images/3-8121f45bc7.jpg)![](https://html.scribdassets.com/97ebbo680fs0ulz/images/3-8121f45bc7.jpg)
  
  ad [Download to read ad-free](https://www.scribd.com/oauth/signup?behavior_tag=download&doc_id=929888800)
  
  
  
  Date/Time of Evidence Collection:
  
  
  
  Location:
  
  
  
  Parties Involved:
  
  6\. Evidence Collecon
  
  
  
  Evidence ID:
  
  
  
  Description of Evidence:
  
  (device type, serial number, make, model)
  
  
  
  Acquisition Method:
  
  (bit-by-bit imaging, logical copy, live capture, etc.)
  
  
  
  Hash Values:
  
  (MD5, SHA256 to verify integrity)
  
  
  
  Chain of Custody:
  
  (who handled evidence and when)
  
  7\. Tools and Methodology
  
  
  
  Forensic tools used (e.g., Autopsy, FTK Imager, EnCase, Wireshark)
  
  
  
  Operating procedure followed (step-by-step process)
  
  
  
  Any standards referenced (e.g., NIST guidelines)
  
  8
  
  . Analysis and Findings
  
  
  
  Detailed observations (e.g., recovered files, network logs, deleted data)
  
  
  
  Timeline reconstruction
  
  
  
  Correlation of artifacts
  
  
  
  Screenshots (if necessary)
  
  9\. Conclusion
  
  
  
  Summarize findings
  
  
  
  State whether objectives were met
  
  
  
  Mention if further investigation is recommended
  
  10\. Recommendaons (Oponal)
  
  
  
  Security improvements
  
  
  
  Policy changes
  
